        "What is meant by regional synthesis?",
        "In regional synthesis, all the geographical features of a region are joined to present a complete picture. Presenting a complete picture is its very aim. Regional synthesis means the integrated, holistic study of all physical and human elements of a region (region) as one complete unit — not in fragments. For example, while studying the Ganga plain, its soil, climate, rivers, crops, population, towns and transport are all seen together. This approach comes from Vidal de la Blache's French tradition, where the concept of 'pays' (small natural region) was central. Its importance is that it gives the complete picture of a region, making balanced regional planning possible. In the exam, giving the definition with one example makes a complete answer.",
