        "Explain the meaning of areal differentiation.",
        "Areal differentiation studies the features that make one region different from another. Understanding the differences between regions is its main task. Areal differentiation means the study of differences between different areas of the Earth — 'why one area differs from another'. It was propounded by Richard Hartshorne. For example — why Rajasthan is desert-like and Kerala humid; why the Ganga plain is densely settled and the Himalayas sparsely. This approach makes geography a 'chorological science' — the task of geography is to understand the uniqueness of areas. It helps identify causes of regional disparities, which is useful in planning to remove inequalities. Regional synthesis sees 'wholeness', areal differentiation sees 'difference' — the two complement each other.",
