        "Describe the factors affecting industrial location.",
        "Where an industry is set up depends on: raw material supply, power, nearness to market, cheap and skilled workers, transport facilities, money (capital) and government policies. Factors affecting industrial location fall into two groups. Natural factors — (1) raw material: industries using heavy raw material locate near the source (iron and steel); (2) power resources: cheap electricity/coal. Human factors — (3) market: nearness saves transport cost; (4) labour: skilled and cheap workers; (5) transport: facility to bring raw material and send finished goods; (6) capital: money for investment. According to Weber, transport cost is decisive among these. Agglomeration also gathers industries at one place — mutual benefit of facilities.",
