        "What are tertiary activities? Give examples.",
        "Work in which services are given instead of making goods — like trade, transport, communication, banking, education, health and tourism — is called tertiary activity. Tertiary activities are those economic activities in which services are given instead of producing goods — they are 'intangible', cannot be touched, only experienced. Examples — trade (buying-selling service), transport (carrying people/goods), communication (carrying information), banking-insurance, education, health, tourism, administration. They are called 'tertiary' because they come after primary (production) and secondary (processing) — the 'service sector'. In developed countries more than 50% of workers are in this sector — the modern economy has become a 'service economy'.",
