                   "Environmental pollution means the release of substances and energy from waste products of human activities into the environment.",
                   "There are four major types of pollution — air pollution, water pollution, land pollution and noise pollution.",
                   "The main sources of air pollution are industries, vehicles, thermal power plants and domestic fuels; major pollutants are carbon monoxide, sulphur dioxide, nitrogen oxides and suspended particulate matter (SPM).",
                   "Effects of air pollution include respiratory diseases, acid rain, smog and global warming.",
                   "The main sources of water pollution are industrial effluents, agricultural runoff (fertilisers and pesticides) and domestic sewage.",
                   "Effects of water pollution include water-borne diseases like cholera and typhoid, and harm to aquatic life.",
                   "Land pollution is caused by solid waste, chemicals and pesticides; it reduces soil fertility and quality.",
                   "Noise pollution is location-specific and its intensity declines with distance from the noise source; it is measured in decibels.",
                   "The main sources of noise pollution are industries, means of transport, loudspeakers and construction work.",
                   "Effects of noise pollution include loss of hearing, mental stress, disturbed sleep and reduced efficiency.",
                   "Towns and cities are the major producers of solid waste, which includes metal pieces, glassware, plastic containers, polythene bags, ash and similar items.",
